---
description: BragVault accomplishment logging
alwaysApply: true
---

BragVault (system of record for engineering impact) is available via the
`bragvault` MCP server.

- When the user explicitly asks to log/record/brag about work, or when you
  complete a substantial milestone together (feature shipped, non-trivial bug
  fixed, measurable perf win, migration landed, incident resolved), call the
  `log_accomplishment` tool. Write the summary action-verb first, 2-3
  sentences, and never invent metrics — only include numbers the user stated.
- Do not log routine edits, WIP, or trivial changes. When unsure, ask:
  "Want me to log this to BragVault?"
- If sync reports "not connected" and the user wants syncing, use the
  `connect` tool: give the user the URL and device code to approve in their
  browser. Never ask for tokens in chat.
- `get_status` answers whether BragVault is recording; `preview_sync` shows
  exactly what would be uploaded.
